WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:09.150
This tutorial connects Google Drive, so every video you export uploads itself and comes back with a link you can share. It takes about two minutes.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:14.220
Open Settings with the cog at the bottom left, and choose Google Drive.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:26.060
Press Connect Google Drive. Your browser opens on Google’s own sign-in page. Pick your account, and press Allow. The app can only see the folders and files it creates itself, never the rest of your Drive.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:37.490
Back in the app, give the parent folder a name and press Create parent folder. Everything the app uploads goes inside this one folder. You can move or rename it in Drive later, and the app keeps following it.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:46.270
Now press Test Google Drive now. It creates a folder, uploads a file, reads it back, and removes both. Six ticks means it is working.

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:57.790
Finally, make a folder in your library. A green message confirms the same folder now exists in Google Drive, with a button to open it. Videos you file there upload into it when you export.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:05.380
That is Google Drive connected. Every export now uploads itself into the matching folder, and gives you a link to share.
